SysInfo is distributed under the terms of the GNU General Public License
version 3 (GPL-3.0-only). The full text of the GPL v3 is provided in the
accompanying file GPL-3.0.txt.

Corresponding source code for this build is available at:
    https://github.com/1minEpowMinX/SysInfo

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party component: Qt
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product uses the Qt framework (version @Qt6_VERSION@).

    Copyright (C) The Qt Company Ltd. and other Qt contributors.

The Qt modules used in this build are licensed as follows:

  Qt6Core, Qt6Gui, Qt6Widgets, Qt6Network, Qt6Svg, Qt6WebSockets
      GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 (LGPL-3.0-only)

  Qt6HttpServer
      GNU General Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0-only)

The LGPL v3 incorporates the terms of the GPL v3, supplemented by additional
permissions granted by the LGPL v3. Accordingly, two license documents
accompany this distribution:

    GPL-3.0.txt     - GNU General Public License, version 3
    LGPL-3.0.txt    - GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3

The Qt libraries are delivered as separate dynamically-linked shared libraries:
on Windows, one .dll per module named above, together with the platform and
plugin .dll files shipped alongside the executable; equivalent .so/.dylib files
on Linux/macOS.

As permitted by LGPL v3 section 4(d)(1), this satisfies the "suitable shared
library mechanism" requirement: you may replace the LGPL-licensed Qt shared
libraries with a modified or recompiled version of the same Qt major.minor
release (@Qt6_VERSION_MAJOR@.@Qt6_VERSION_MINOR@.x) by overwriting the corresponding files in the
installation directory, and SysInfo will continue to load and run with the
replaced libraries.

Complete and corresponding source code for the exact Qt version used in this
build is published by The Qt Company at:

    https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/@Qt6_VERSION_MAJOR@.@Qt6_VERSION_MINOR@/@Qt6_VERSION@/single/
    https://code.qt.io/

No modifications have been made to the Qt source code by the SysInfo
project; the Qt binaries ship as produced by the official Qt @Qt6_VERSION@ release.

The Qt modules and plugins listed above additionally incorporate third-party
components, each under a license of its own rather than under the license of
the module it is built into. Every one of them, with its version, copyright,
license and the library it is delivered in, is named in the accompanying file:

    THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt

which also carries the full text of every license it names.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party component: LLVM runtime libraries
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Windows builds produced with the llvm-mingw toolchain ship the LLVM C++ runtime
alongside the executable:

    libc++.dll      - LLVM C++ standard library
    libunwind.dll   - LLVM unwinder

    Copyright (c) The LLVM Project contributors.

Both are part of the LLVM Project and are licensed under the Apache License
version 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions. The full text is provided in the accompanying
file LLVM-Apache-2.0.txt.

Source code for the LLVM Project is published at:

    https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project

Builds produced with another toolchain link that toolchain's own C++ runtime
instead and do not ship these files.

